**BILL NO. 1.659, OF 2011**

**(From the Federal Senate)**

**PROPOSAL FOR A LAW**

*Creating the Small and Medium Citrus Producers Support Program (Proap Citros).*

The National Congress decrees:

**ARTICLE 1:** The Executive Power is authorized to create the Small and Medium Citrus Producers Support Program (Proap Citros).

**ARTICLE 2:** This Law shall enter into force on the date of its publication.

**ARTICLE 3:** This Law aims to:

I. Ensure the competitive insertion of small and medium citrus producers into the market;

II. Encourage the formation of mechanisms for integrating the productive chain, involving the agro-industrial sector;

III. Strengthen the domestic market for citrus and its derived products, including through official marketing campaigns focused on improving the health of the Brazilian population;

IV. Expand access for small and medium citrus producers to banking credit mechanisms;

V. Provide financial assistance to producers for the purpose of implementing and financing their crops;

VI. Develop alternative outlets and storage solutions for production;

VII. Encourage initiatives for verticalization of production through producer associations;

VIII. Provide specialized technical assistance, focusing on generating income for the producer;

IX. Improve the educational conditions of small producers and their dependents, as well as establish and expand professional training, particularly addressing phytosanitary and property management issues;

X. Support research for the generation and transfer of technology, including for the production of new varieties;

XI. Encourage organic production systems;

XII. Provide assistance for sustainable use of natural resources.

**ARTICLE 4:** The Executive Power, through its official communication agencies, shall develop an extensive national marketing education campaign on television and radio, aiming to increase citrus consumption, highlighting the fruit's functional benefits for consumer health and promoting preventive medicine through diet.

**ARTICLE 5:** The program's beneficiaries shall be selected based on the annual gross income of the applicant.

**ARTICLE 6:** The establishment of the Citrus Arbitration Chamber (Consecitrus) is authorized, with the purpose of setting parameters for defining the prices of citrus and its derived products.

**§ 1:** The organization and functioning of the Citrus Arbitration Chamber shall be regulated by the Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock and Supply (MAPA).

**§ 2:** The Chamber shall be composed of one representative from small and medium citrus producers, one rural worker from the citrus industry, one representative from citrus processing companies, and one representative from the Federal Government.

**ARTICLE 7:** This Law shall enter into force on the date of its publication.

