(a) Brazilian mineral and energy policies and models;
(b) Institutional structure and role of agents in the mineral and energy sectors;
(c) Conventional and alternative energy sources;
(d) Research and exploration of mineral and energy resources;
(e) Forms of access to mineral resources; mining companies;
(f) Energy resource pricing policies;
(g) Marketing and industrialization of minerals;
(h) Promotion of mining activity;
(i) Legal regime of mineral and water resources;
(j) Management, planning, and control of water resources; legal regime of public and private waters.

The unique paragraph of Article 32, stating that the thematic fields or areas of activity of each Permanent Commission encompass government agencies and programs related to them, and their budgetary monitoring, also allows the Commission on Mines and Energy to oversee ANP's activities.

This PFC aims to verify the correct collection and transfer of financial compensation from the exploration of oil and natural gas, which are Union natural resources. This collection and transfer originates from the very Federal Constitution, in Article 20, paragraph 1.

The following is the relevant constitutional provision:

'Article 20. [...] § 1. It is guaranteed, in accordance with the law, to the States, the Federal District, and municipalities, as well as to public administration organs, the right to receive, in the form established by law, part of the net revenue from oil and natural gas exploration and production.'

It follows that royalties can range from 5% to 10% of the production value of oil or natural gas."

